     You mentioned this earlier too, but it is backwards.  The
chance of leaving bones increases with depth.  However, fewer
games overall--and in particular, fewer games ending with the
character's death--manage to get deeper so the chance for seeing
such bones tends to get smaller.  (In other words, most deaths
occur before getting that far.)

     It's been mentioned that D0.1 through D0.3 must have come
from wizard mode, assuming that the range of D0.1 through D0.39
for Hearse is accurate.  D0.29 through D0.39 can't be from plain
nethack either.  Main dungeon is limited to at most 29 levels,
and the deepest one would be the non-bones-eligible Castle rather
than D0.29.  So your own set of D0.4 through D0.28 is expected.

     Slash'em extends the main dungeon and shortens Gehennom,
so a range of D levels up to 39 is plausible there.  I don't
remember whether any of Lethe/Heck/Hell patches also did that.


